{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('state.json'))\nfor k in st['knowledge']:\n    if k.get('id')=='983e6d23976b4e4e9eff6a3987874db1-knowledge-0':\n        h=k.get('history')\n        print(json.dumps(h,indent=1)[:4000])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"id\": \"983e6d23976b4e4e9eff6a3987874db1-knowledge-0\",\n  \"revision\": 1,\n  \"kind\": \"fact\",\n  \"statement\": \"A VerifyLeader request queued while a leader's main loop is stalled past its lease is answered without success once the stall ends, even though a successor has been elected in the meantime. Across eight trials the stalled leader held only Leader state for every 1ms sample while another server led at term 3 (first seen at 345-464ms), yet the queued verify returned non-nil in all eight: seven times 'leadership lost while committing log' and twice 'node is not the leader', at 600-602ms, the moment the stall released the main loop; the concurrent Apply failed the same way. The endpoints show the lease case was already ready when the loop resumed, so leadership was given up before the non-voter's acknowledgement could be counted, which is ordering rather than the eligibility rule that the verify quorum itself violates.\",\n  \"conditions\": \"Three voters plus one non-voter, the leader partitioned so only the non-voter is reachable, HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 200ms, a 600ms stall that blocks StoreLogs on the leader's main thread while a client Apply is in flight, in-memory transports in one process.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n   \"verify_leader\",\n   \"quorum_size\",\n   \"lease_check\",\n   \"lease_check_granularity\",\n   \"start_stop_repl\",\n   \"notify_all\",\n   \"update_last_appended\",\n   \"verify_vote\"\n  ],\n  \"executions\": {\n   \"2e5f37f634834b8197227626ed6d99b7\": [\n    1,\n    3,\n    5,\n    7,\n    9,\n    11,\n    13,\n    15\n   ]\n  },\n  \"knowledge\": [],\n  \"operation_id\": \"983e6d23976b4e4e9eff6a3987874db1\",\n  \"correction\": \"The trigger is corrected rather than extended: the behaviour was described as a VerifyLeader call handed back while Shutdown is in progress, and the revision shows the same strand for calls issued after Shutdown has already returned, so the operative condition is the buffered verifyCh with no drainer and a future without ShutdownCh, not the timing of the shutdown. The earlier racing evidence is kept and the post-shutdown counts are added.\",\n  \"recorded_uses\": [],\n  \"affected_uses\": []\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nR1=\\\"a1933fdba3e74bd1b98cd6e8dcd138c4\\\"; R2=\\\"b3b821a061f346a1aa27e3fee5e44cb9\\\"; RS=\\\"2e5f37f634834b8197227626ed6d99b7\\\"\nstall_stmt=(\\\"A VerifyLeader request queued while a leader's main loop is stalled past its lease is answered without success once the stall ends, even though a successor has been elected in the meantime. Across eight trials the stalled leader held only Leader state for every 1ms sample while another server led at term 3 (first seen at 345-464ms), yet the queued verify returned non-nil in all eight: seven times 'leadership lost while committing log' and twice 'node is not the leader', at 600-602ms, the moment the stall released the main loop; the concurrent Apply failed the same way. The endpoints show the lease case was already ready when the loop resumed, so leadership was given up before the non-voter's acknowledgement could be counted, which is ordering rather than the eligibility rule that the verify quorum itself violates.\\\")\nshutdown_stmt=(\\\"VerifyLeader can hand back a future that nothing will ever complete, because the request waits in the buffered verifyCh that no reader drains once the run loop has exited and the future itself carries no shutdown channel to unblock on. The trigger does not require racing Shutdown: calls made after Shutdown has already returned strand about half the time, since the closed shutdown channel and a send into the 64-slot verifyCh are both selectable. In the revision, post-shutdown VerifyLeader calls were answered 4, 3 and 3 of 8 times and left unanswered 4, 5 and 5 times (14 of 24 stranded), while Barrier and Apply answered all 48 of their post-shutdown calls with ErrRaftShutdown, which matches verifyCh being buffered and applyCh unbuffered by default. The earlier receipt shows the racing form as well, leaving 9 and 41 of 64 futures incomplete in two of three trials with none in the control.\\\")\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Repaired a knowledge mislabel from the previous turn. The correction that added the post-shutdown evidence was submitted against the stall-route entry (983e6d23976b4e4e9eff6a3987874db1-knowledge-0) instead of the shutdown entry (c27ce810268e4535bf01c8870a682db4-knowledge-0), so the stall Fact was overwritten by the shutdown premise. This update restores the stall premise under its own id with the wording of its revision 1 and re-points its execution at the stall receipt, and it applies the intended refinement to the shutdown entry under its own id: the operative condition is the buffered verifyCh plus a future without ShutdownCh rather than the timing of the shutdown. Both entries now describe their own behaviour, both changed premises are recorded, and no measurement is withdrawn.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"983e6d23976b4e4e9eff6a3987874db1-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\\\"statement\\\":stall_stmt,\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Three voters plus one non-voter, the leader partitioned so only the non-voter is reachable, HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 200ms, a 600ms stall that blocks StoreLogs on the leader's main thread while a client Apply is in flight, in-memory transports in one process.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"verify_leader\\\",\\\"quorum_size\\\",\\\"lease_check\\\",\\\"lease_check_granularity\\\",\\\"start_stop_repl\\\",\\\"notify_all\\\",\\\"update_last_appended\\\",\\\"verify_vote\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{RS:[1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15]},\n   \\\"changed_premise\\\":(\\\"The premise is restored, not changed: revision 2 of this entry recorded the shutdown-strand premise, which belongs to c27ce810268e4535bf01c8870a682db4-knowledge-0, so this revision re-states the stall-route premise of revision 1 and re-points the executions at that receipt.\\\"),\n   \\\"affected_uses\\\":[]},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"c27ce810268e4535bf01c8870a682db4-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\\\"statement\\\":shutdown_stmt,\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Single-voter Raft instance, HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 50ms, in-memory transport in one process, BatchApplyCh not set; 64 concurrent calls issued just before Shutdown in the first receipt and 128 with an interleaved shutdown plus 8 post-shutdown calls in the revision.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_verify_future\\\",\\\"defer_error_block\\\",\\\"verify_channel_buffer\\\",\\\"shutdown_close\\\",\\\"api_barrier_future\\\",\\\"api_apply_future\\\",\\\"apply_channel_unbuffered\\\",\\\"test_todo_stuck\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{R1:[1,7,13,19], R2:[1,7,13,3,9,15]},\n   \\\"changed_premise\\\":(\\\"The trigger is corrected rather than extended: the behaviour was first described as a VerifyLeader call handed back while Shutdown is in progress, and the revision shows the same strand for calls issued after Shutdown has already returned, so the operative condition is the buffered verifyCh with no drainer and a future without ShutdownCh, not the timing of the shutdown. The racing evidence of the first receipt is kept and the post-shutdown counts are added.\\\"),\n   \\\"affected_uses\\\":[]}]}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
